# 13. KOSH Memory Layer

KOSH acts as persistent session memory.

It stores:

- Request summary
- Selected persona
- Selected playbooks
- Files touched
- Sonar result
- Security result
- Token usage
- Decisions made
- Audit verdict
- Known recurring mistakes

Purpose:

- Avoid repeating previous mistakes
- Preserve engineering context
- Support audit trails
- Improve future task routing

**Speaker Notes:**  
KOSH turns one-off AI responses into organizational learning.

